# Garagewiki Chat API — Environment Variables

Set these in your Vercel project (Project Settings → Environment Variables):

## LLM provider (required)
| Key                | Purpose                                  | Example                              |
|--------------------|------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|
| `OPENAI_API_KEY`   | Your provider API key (OpenAI, OpenRouter, xAI, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint) | `sk-...` |
| `OPENAI_MODEL`     | Model to call                              | `gpt-4o-mini` (default)              |
| `OPENAI_BASE_URL`  | Base URL of the LLM provider API           | `https://api.openai.com/v1` / `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1` |

## Data source (required)
| Key                 | Purpose                                  | Example                                      |
|---------------------|------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|
| `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` | Supabase project URL                     | `https://cvojoqdggklxdfpxojpz.supabase.co`  |
| `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` | Supabase anon key (read-only access to approved rows) | `sb_pub...` |

## Optional
| Key        | Purpose                                  | Default                                              |
|------------|------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|
| `SITE_URL` | Where the community wiki lives           | `https://gearguide-tau.vercel.app`                   |

## Configuring a provider
### OpenAI
1. Get a key at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
2. Set `OPENAI_API_KEY`, leave `OPENAI_MODEL` and `OPENAI_BASE_URL` at defaults.

### OpenRouter (free-ish tier, easy to start)
1. Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys
2. Set `OPENAI_API_KEY=<your key>`, `OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`,
   `OPENAI_MODEL=google/gemini-2.0-flash-exp` (or any OpenRouter model).

### Anthropic
Anthropic's native endpoint is **not** OpenAI-compatible, so it requires an
OpenRouter key or a proxy. Either use OpenRouter above, or run a tiny proxy.
